<title>CROATIA: Croatian stocks closed mixed.</title>
<headline>Croatian stocks closed mixed.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatian stocks were mixed on Tuesday with slight recovery among some of the blue chips.</p>
<p>* Out of eight issues traded, three were up, four were down and one remained flat.</p>
<p>* Volume was down to 1,649 shares, while turnover was up at 2.2 million kuna.</p>
<p>* The biggest gainer, drug firm Pliva, gained 995 kuna to close at 13,000 on volume of 106 shares.</p>
<p>* The biggest loser, cable producer Elka, lost 25 kuna to close at 195.</p>
<p>* Most actively traded issue was Zagrebacka Banka with 550 shares sold. Bank shares edged down 10 kuna to 980.</p>
<p>($1=5.5635 kuna)</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
